WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.801
-Our first guest tonight is
a two-time Emmy Award-winning

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:04.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
actress you know from her work
as Karen Walker

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:05.205 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
on "Will &amp; Grace."

00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:09.009
New episodes air Thursday nights
at 9:30, here on NBC.

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:09.943 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:15.482 line:92%
-♪♪ Good riddance, goodbye ♪♪

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:24.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
♪♪ Every trick of his,
you're onto ♪♪

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:28.461 line:92%
♪♪ But fools will be fools ♪♪

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:35.235 line:92%
♪♪ And where's he gone to? ♪♪

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:36.469 line:92%
-Please welcome back to the show

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:38.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
our friend Megan Mullally,
everyone!

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:41.541 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:48.248 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:54.421 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:56.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
Welcome back!
-Thank you!

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:58.758 size:84% position:42%
Thanks for having me.
-Delighted to have you.

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:01.161
Do you like when you get to
show off your musical chops

00:01:01.161 --> 00:01:03.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
in an episode like that?
-Well, I mean, I know

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:04.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
everybody was probably
expecting jokes,

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:09.369
and then I started singing,
but I think, like, pretty much,

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:12.405 line:92%
like 10 people know that I sing.

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:13.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I kind of started
as a singer,

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.676
and I've done Broadway musicals
and stuff like that.

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:18.778 line:92%
So it was so nice of the writers

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:22.148 size:78% position:39%
to write this episode
where I get to sing.

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:23.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's great!
-It's pretty cool, yeah.

00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:26.086 size:84% position:42%
-And you're actually
coming here to New York

00:01:26.086 --> 00:01:28.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
to perform with --
you have a partner.

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:29.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-A singing duo.

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:32.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nancy and Beth.
-Nancy and Beth.

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:34.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is Stephanie Hunt.
That's me.

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:37.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we have
this really fun band.

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:38.231 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We sing in harmony,

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:41.768
and every song is choreographed
by me from top to bottom.

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:43.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we wear
little matching outfits.

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:45.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we have five pieces
behind us.

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:47.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's this really cool band.
It's hard to describe.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's just very celebratory.
and different.

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:51.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's awesome.
Is it great to return

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:54.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
to those roots and
be onstage, singing like that?

00:01:54.214 --> 00:01:54.848 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:58.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
The band, in many ways,
is kind of my favorite thing,

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:01.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
just because,
with Stephanie and I,

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's like two little girls
playing, you know.

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:05.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-It's just pure creativity.

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:06.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you do have
a lot of control

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:08.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you're not doing it
as a television show.

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:10.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
When you actually just go out
in front of an audience,

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:12.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
it must just feel so freeing.
-Yeah, it's fun,

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:14.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
because we call it
punk vaudeville sometimes,

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:17.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
because there's no way
to make up our own category.

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:19.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
But we get out there
and the songs --

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:20.473 line:92%
the songs are really sharp.

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:24.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then it all just
falls to pieces in between.

00:02:24.077 --> 00:02:25.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughing ] Uh-huh.
-You know?

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:27.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We're like,
"Now what do we do?"

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:29.983
We don't have anything planned.
-That's great.

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:31.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's great.
-You just went through

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:34.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
the awards circuit,
you were at the Golden Globes.

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:35.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you have a good time
at the Globes?

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:37.790
-Did you get to bump into people
that you were excited to see?

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:39.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did. I've got the secret.
So, if you're --

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:41.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you're ever going to
present the Golden Globes --

00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:44.230
and I'm sure most of you will...
-Yeah.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.232 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:48.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
...go -- just hang out
in the greenroom.

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:51.838
Like, don't go sit there,
just go straight backstage,

00:02:51.838 --> 00:02:53.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
through an alley,
sit in the greenroom,

00:02:53.573 --> 00:02:55.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
and wait until it's your time,
and then leave,

00:02:55.642 --> 00:02:58.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
because, you know, you get to,
like, people-watch.

00:02:58.311 --> 00:03:01.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was standing there,
talking to --

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:02.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is my favorite thing
that happened.

00:03:02.649 --> 00:03:03.950 line:92%
I was talking to Sam Elliott,

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
who is really tight
with my husband,

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:07.187 line:92%
if you can imagine that much --

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:08.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Your husband, Nick Offerman,
and Sam Elliott.

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:10.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, Nick Offerman.
-That makes perfect sense.

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:12.258 size:88% position:44%
-That much testosterone.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:15.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like ultra man, you know?
-Did they meet, like,

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:17.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
chopping down trees
in the woods?

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:20.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, exactly.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.202 line:92%
And so I was talking to Sam,

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:25.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Harrison Ford wandered up
to say hello to Sam.

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:28.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know him.
Sam introduced me.

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:29.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said, "Hello."
And I said, "you know what?

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:32.378
You were one of my all-time
favorite guests on 'Letterman.'

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:35.448
You were so funny, because
he would ask you a question,

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:38.484 line:92%
and you would just go, 'No.'"

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:39.052 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.052 --> 00:03:41.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, he had this weird thing
going with Letterman.

00:03:41.955 --> 00:03:44.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he goes, "Oh!
How is Dave?"

00:03:44.257 --> 00:03:47.026
And I was like, "I don't know."
And he said...

00:03:47.026 --> 00:03:49.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
..."I hope he's well."

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:52.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he said, "Oh, I thought
you were a writer."

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:56.369
And I said, "No, I'm an actress.
I just presented."

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:58.238 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And he goes, "Ohh!"

00:03:58.238 --> 00:03:59.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "I'm
on a television show.

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:03.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
You wouldn't know."
And he goes, "Oh, gosh. Oh!"

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:07.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said, [Baby talk]
"Harrison made a boo-boo."

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:09.382 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:10.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Normal voice ]
And he literally went,

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:15.121 align:start size:94% position:6%
[Baby talk[ "He did."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:16.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
"He did make a boo-boo."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:19.292
[ Normal voice ] And I thought,
"I love this guy."

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:22.061
-That's the greatest interaction
you possibly could've had.

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:24.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He went full baby talk.
-Wow!

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:25.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-What a jackpot!

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:28.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know.
-Also, when you meet somebody

00:04:28.034 --> 00:04:31.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
who is a giant icon like that,
it's so great

00:04:31.204 --> 00:04:33.206 size:81% position:41%
when they're the one
who makes the mistake.

00:04:33.206 --> 00:04:34.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Totes.
-Because usually,

00:04:34.307 --> 00:04:36.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
the lower-status person
gets nervous and screws up.

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:38.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But he blew it.

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:39.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then you got to
reap the reward.

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:41.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, I mean,
it was so delightful.

00:04:41.748 --> 00:04:43.616 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. That's just great.
And then you hosted,

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:44.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you were wonderful
at the SAG Awards.

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:46.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that's very nice of you.
I had a lot of fun.

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:47.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did you enjoy that?
-I did.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:51.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had, you know, great --
Everybody was great,

00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:57.397
and I had a lot of fun and,
you know, cute clothes and...

00:04:57.397 --> 00:04:58.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I don't know.

00:04:58.431 --> 00:05:01.467 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You got to --
You sort of made fun

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:03.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
of some people --
Emma stone, Lady Gaga.

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:05.405 size:75% position:38%
Fun "making fun of."
-But in a nice way,

00:05:05.405 --> 00:05:07.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I don't want to do
anything mean-spirited.

00:05:07.507 --> 00:05:08.374 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-It was very friendly.

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:09.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
But did you run into anybody
backstage?

00:05:09.776 --> 00:05:11.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I said that Lady Gaga
did my eyeliner,

00:05:11.644 --> 00:05:12.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
that she'd been
doing my eyeliner

00:05:12.812 --> 00:05:14.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the last 15 years,
that she just --

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:17.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
She just can do anything,
was the gist.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:18.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I went back --
I got backstage,

00:05:18.518 --> 00:05:22.188
like, right after the monologue,
and she was standing there

00:05:22.188 --> 00:05:24.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
and she was like, "Oh, my God!
That was so great.

00:05:24.691 --> 00:05:25.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're so funny."
And blah blah blah.

00:05:25.858 --> 00:05:28.227
And she was super nice.
Like, really normal nice.

00:05:28.227 --> 00:05:31.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"Oh, good, thank you.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:32.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, you know,
you're the real thing.

00:05:32.965 --> 00:05:35.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I'm with Tony Bennett,
your voice --"

00:05:35.001 --> 00:05:37.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, nobody has ever told her
she can sing.

00:05:37.136 --> 00:05:40.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
So I was like, "I'm really --

00:05:40.373 --> 00:05:42.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
really gonna blow her away
with this one."

00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:44.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And she was so nice.

00:05:44.344 --> 00:05:47.280
She goes, "Well, you should come
see my jazz show in Vegas.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:48.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, it's
all that kind of music."

00:05:48.348 --> 00:05:50.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I thought, "I'd love to."
And I said, "You know,

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:52.418 size:78% position:39%
I feel like I'm gonna
call you Stephanie."

00:05:52.418 --> 00:05:54.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she said,
"You can call me Stephanie!"

00:05:54.587 --> 00:05:56.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, isn't that nice?
-That's really nice.

00:05:56.622 --> 00:05:57.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because that's her name.
-Yeah.

00:05:57.657 --> 00:05:59.759
That is her name,
for anybody who doesn't know --

00:05:59.759 --> 00:06:02.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
because otherwise,
you sound like a crazy person.

00:06:02.428 --> 00:06:03.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:06:03.096 --> 00:06:06.165
"I'd like to call you Pam!"
-"I'm gonna call you Bill."

00:06:06.165 --> 00:06:07.166 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:09.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
She is a lovely person.
-She was so nice.

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:11.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And that is -- I mean,
I think -- the only reason

00:06:11.904 --> 00:06:15.141
to go to those shows is to have
those, like, actual in --

00:06:15.141 --> 00:06:17.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, sort of nice moments
backstage that are --

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:19.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, backstage is
where it's at, man.

00:06:19.679 --> 00:06:21.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
just walking by people,

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:23.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
just like, "Hey!"
it's great.

00:06:23.383 --> 00:06:25.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I love it.

